:{"commit_sha":"1fe00b13fae48b8d7cac58cf0f3dd684e8c9f8df","position":"1787023900128767001-f282d9ce-6f57-41da-b19c-8774808b5339"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ecde0c0ef08d292aa2a5a3c41f6f47bd953adc6126f42f964ea27dec6eb96b07","event_uuid":"ec5892b1-284b-41a8-98e9-34dced0177b5","position":{"commit_sha":"7c814f63443622a1d9b35d1bacd292aee1fc68fb","position":"1787023904628478001-ec5892b1-284b-41a8-98e9-34dced0177b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8f3d97814ab266d4df376e83fcaf3a6e55931f0c654c55d52e9b90a6853f27f9","event_uuid":"3c8c2684-4c0a-4400-b970-9e1c2ec2cc9a","position":{"commit_sha":"a12a38237064418c0d21484a45ee674bdd89c2ec","position":"1787023919851594001-3c8c2684-4c0a-4400-b970-9e1c2ec2cc9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787022487467870001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0bdbe286-cac5-4055-b3b7-8526d1d9b7dd","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb"},{"link_uuid":"af1f3bf6-112c-4e6f-bd3e-af8c29dfad4e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"},{"link_uuid":"f282d9ce-6f57-41da-b19c-8774808b5339","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nCurrent recovery lives inside the facade and only repairs interrupted creates. A crash after the retired tombstone replacement but before the live replacement leaves the same exact identity live and retired. That partial state is detectable and safely completable, but construction-time or preview-time repair would violate read-only operations. The rich-text handler also still mutates an entry obtained from `all_bindings()`.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract incomplete-operation recovery behind the facade, cut the production rich-text caller to S2s narrow operation, and add journal-free interrupted-retirement completion at the validated write-bearing reconcile boundary. A durable tombstone is the authoritative retirement intent. Recovery removes the redundant live forward/reverse pair only when tombstone, forward, and reverse identities agree exactly; repeat is a no-op, and all ambiguity safety-aborts. Only explicit `unretire` removes that intent; a later automatic 200/`clear_absent`/same-key confirm does not implicitly resurrect a tombstoned identity.\n\n## Plan\n1. Move keyed/keyless create recovery into `binding_recovery.py` without changing label forms, immutable known-key handling, three-miss plus 3600-second conjunction, per-entry failure collection, or continue behavior.\n2. Add a pure classifier for interrupted retirement states and a repository-backed completion operation. Require exact local id and Jira key agreement in tombstone, forward entry, and reverse entry.\n3. Invoke completion after the immutable configuration operation snapshot, provider/config preflight, exclusive pass ownership, and under-lock staleness validation, but before any remote issue fetch, binding walk, differ, or lifecycle mutation in that pass. Load, construction, reconcile-check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filtered operations remain read-only.\n4. Treat the tombstone as the committed side of the retired-first protocol. `absent_404_count`, a later 200, `clear_absent`, or same-key `bind_confirm` in a historical overlap is not a revocation signal; explicit `unretire` removes the tombstone, after which no completion candidate exists. If live replacement fails, retain the overlap and safety-abort for a later retry.\n5. Replace `apply_handlers.py` mutation-through-`all_bindings()` with S2s facade operation after RP-04 S3 has landed its scoped-runtime changes to that file.\n6. Finalize `docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md` when the behavior lands: record tombstone authority versus explicit unretire, the before-observation repair boundary, intentional behavior change, rollback, and the explicit ban on broad tickets-branch staging.\n\n## Dependencies / coordination\nThis story depends directly on RP-02 S1 and S2. Its `apply_handlers.py` and live-boundary edits must be rebased after RP-04 S3 (`talismanic-profitable-isopod`) closes. That cross-root execution condition is recorded as a soft relation because Rebars hierarchy resolver would otherwise promote a child edge into an unnecessarily broad RP-02-epic → RP-04-epic blocker; overlapping file impact remains visible.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- Fault-cut tests create the real retired-first/live-failed overlap, reopen a fresh store, execute pre-observation live recovery, and assert coherent retired-only bytes and repeat no-op.\n- Mismatch tables vary each identity, missing reverse/live entries, corrupt live bytes, and replacement failure; the oracle is zero guessed deletion plus a typed safety abort.\n- Intent-order tests cover a historical overlap whose stale live record was cleared/reconfirmed to the same key: the tombstone still completes. An explicit `unretire` removes the tombstone and prevents repair.\n- Read-only surface tests spy on `os.replace`/repository save across construction, check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filter modes and assert zero calls.\n- Existing create recovery/index-lag and rich-reemit suites remain exact behavior oracles.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDisabling the pre-observation recovery call restores the prior detectable overlap; coherent stores are never rewritten. The public recovery method and failure tally remain compatible. Rollback of the rich-text call returns to the shallow query path without a format change. No journal, eager recovery, broad publication, automatic resurrection, or remote rollback is added.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given the real retired-first/live-replace fault cut, the next validated write-bearing pass completes repair before remote issue observation and retains the tombstone.\n- [ ] Repeating completion is a no-op; any tombstone/forward/reverse mismatch, corrupt live file, or replace failure leaves recoverable evidence and safety-aborts without unrelated mutation.\n- [ ] Construction, load, reconcile-check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filtered runs perform zero recovery writes.\n- [ ] A later automatic 200/`clear_absent`/same-key confirm does not override a durable tombstone; explicit `unretire` removes the tombstone and prevents completion.\n- [ ] Keyed pending recovery performs no search; keyless pending requires both three misses and 3600 seconds before unbind; per-entry failures remain loud and nonfatal to other entries.\n- [ ] `apply_handlers.py` uses the narrow rich-emission facade and no production code mutates a binding through `all_bindings()`.\n- [ ] ADR 0099 records the realized repair rule, pre-observation boundary, explicit-unretire reversal, rollback, and prohibition on broad tickets-branch staging.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_recovery.py","reason":"Extract create recovery and exact-match retirement completion."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Expose compatible recovery delegates through the authoritative facade."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"Invoke recovery before remote issue observation at the validated write-bearing boundary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Cut production rich-emission mutation to the narrow facade operation."},{"path":"docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md","reason":"Finalize the realized retirement repair, reversal, ordering, rollback, and staging decisions."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_recovery.py","reason":"Crash-cut, intent-order, idempotency, mismatch, and replace-failure oracles."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py","reason":"Keyless grace and duplicate-prevention regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py","reason":"Production narrow-operation cutover regression."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py","reason":"Pre-observation ordering plus check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filter zero-write tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","5142-4dbf-9469-4672"],["depends_on","fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb"],["parent","5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"],["relates_to","6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp02","reconciler","recovery","tdd"],"ticket_id":"486a-69ef-6370-48ff","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-02 S3 — Recover exact retirement overlaps at the live operation boundary","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_recovery.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Pre-observation retirement crash cut, tombstone intent, explicit unretire, idempotency, mismatch, and replace failure"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Zero recovery writes from check, dry-run, preview, selected, and filtered operations"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_no_resurrection_after_confirmed_delete_3b5f.py","dd_id":"AC5-AC6","dd_text":"Create recovery grace, narrow rich-emission cutover, and tombstone regressions"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC7","dd_text":"Finalized ADR numbering and index integrity"}]},"source_event_uuids":["a0250740-0aa5-4c2b-ae2c-a1d77ad9e02c","0bdbe286-cac5-4055-b3b7-8526d1d9b7dd","af1f3bf6-112c-4e6f-bd3e-af8c29dfad4e","0e6cc29f-1d8f-4825-a8c6-a4ac3ec57a35","d32d1163-3fb1-4814-aaa7-d1af5a7ce1cd","2bb6b2ef-e4b7-4520-bf54-3ddecec43004","f282d9ce-6f57-41da-b19c-8774808b5339","ec5892b1-284b-41a8-98e9-34dced0177b5","3c8c2684-4c0a-4400-b970-9e1c2ec2cc9a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787026539242386001,"uuid":"3e6ba309-a46b-4886-b966-cd5145d13d5f"}